{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Stories From the Hospital", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Bedside Manners", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 11, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past and The Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You often use the Simple Past and the Past Continuous tenses together. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense to refer to the context of a story. It talks about the \u2018background' action, or the longer action. You use it to talk about an action that was in progress in the past.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The anesthetic <span class=\"strong\">was wearing off</span> and the pain <span class=\"strong\">was coming</span> back.</span> <br/><br/>  You can use the Simple Past tense to refer to a shorter action that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer action, or a finished action at specific time in the past.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had</span> the most terrible experience at the hospital a month ago. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She was cleaning up the water when my doctor finally came in to check up on me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He looked perplexed ... and out of the blue, he turned around and walked out of the room. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Suddenly, a bright light appeared over my bed and a ghostly figure was emanating from it.<br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs are two-part verbs consisting of a verb followed by an adverb particle (these look like prepositions, but do not have the same function in phrasal verbs).<br/> In some cases, it is not possible to separate the verb and the particle. These are called <span class=\"italic\">inseparable</span> phrasal verbs.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "It is important to remember that the meaning of a phrasal verb is often very different from the two parts taken separately.<br/><br/> For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Matt <span class=\"strong\">turned up</span> last night</span> (= appeared, not the same as turned + up).<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">To turn up</span> is an inseparable phrasal verb. You cannot put an object between the verb and the particle. It must remain together. <br/><br/> Another example is <span class=\"italic\">to get off</span>. <br/> You can say \u201c<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">get off</span> the bus</span>\u201d, but you cannot say \u201c<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">get</span> the bus <span class=\"strong\">off</span></span>\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A few verbs can be used with both a particle and a preposition, making them <span class=\"strong\">three-part verbs</span>.<br/><br/> For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to run away with</span> (to leave; to escape from)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to watch out for</span> (to be careful for)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">to back out of</span> (to fail to keep a promise)<br/><br/>  Learning phrasal verbs is a lot like learning new vocabulary. You must memorize which phrasal verbs are inseparable and learn their meanings. <br/><br/>  Look at the chart for some more inseparable phrasal verbs and their meanings.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">check up on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"see how someone is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">read up on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"search information on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">look for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">put up with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tolerate\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "She was cleaning up the water when my doctor finally came in to check up on me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had read up on this hospital and heard rumors that it was haunted, but I couldn't believe what I was seeing! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I won't put up with that kind of treatment again!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bizarre", "type": "name"}, {"content": "strange; very unusual", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He had also seen the bizarre light in the distance. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are the words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "anesthetic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a drug that blocks the pain someone is feeling", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must be confused from the anesthetic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "custodian", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person in charge of maintaining a property", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The custodian here could clean up that broken glass on the floor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hoarse", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a rough and unclear voice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: \u201cOf course,\" the old man said in his soft hoarse voice.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "perplexed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "confused and worried", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The girl's story left me baffled and perplexed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "haunted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inhabited or visited by ghosts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The hotel is said to be haunted.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rumor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a story that lacks solid basis and is unlikely to be true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: People have heard of rumors of a supernatural presence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "out of the blue", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to mean that something happens unexpectedly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I was walking to meet you and out of the blue I heard a dog barking.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fangs", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the long pointed teeth that some animals have, for example snakes, dogs, and tigers", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vampires have sharp fangs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to undergo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to experience something that is unpleasant or involves a change", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She'd been admitted to the hospital the day before, to undergo surgery on her knee.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "You look like you've seen a ghost", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to mean someone looks scared or shocked", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hi, Peter. Wow, you look like you've seen a ghost! Are you okay?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le11ob11aud11", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Patch Adams</span> with subtitles in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes on events and new vocabulary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what Patch was like as a doctor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what might have happened to some of the patients he treated if he had not been their doctor.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I watch the movie <span class=\"italic\">Patch Adams</span> with subtitles in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes on new vocabulary.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss what Patch was like as a doctor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss what might have happened to the patients.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about coincidences, strange events, superstitions, and sickness.", "type": 